1
00:00:00,494 --> 00:00:02,664
(Howard:)What are you doing?

2
00:00:02,664 --> 00:00:04,634
(Raj:)It's called Lamaze breathing.

3
00:00:04,633 --> 00:00:07,263
(Raj:)It helps you push.

4
00:00:08,102 --> 00:00:09,372
(Leonard:)Great.

5
00:00:09,371 --> 00:00:10,771
(Howard:)He's pushing
with his uterus.

6
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:15,910
(Raj:)There's got to be a smarter way
of removing it.

7
00:00:15,911 --> 00:00:17,681
(Leonard:)Yeah, this is nothing more
than a physics problem.

8
00:00:17,679 --> 00:00:18,949
(Howard:)Right.

9
00:00:18,947 --> 00:00:20,717
(Sheldon:)Archimedes once said,

10
00:00:20,716 --> 00:00:21,986
"Give me a 'leever' long enough

11
00:00:21,983 --> 00:00:23,483
"and a fulcrum
on which to place it,

12
00:00:23,485 --> 00:00:24,815
and I shall move the world."

13
00:00:24,820 --> 00:00:26,520
(Raj:)Of course.

14
00:00:26,521 --> 00:00:28,221
(Raj:)All we need is to find stuff

15
00:00:28,223 --> 00:00:30,723
to make a "leever" big
enough to fix this.

16
00:00:30,726 --> 00:00:31,956
(Howard:)Exactly.

17
00:00:31,960 --> 00:00:33,130
(Howard:)I'll bet there's
something around here

18
00:00:33,128 --> 00:00:34,728
(Howard:)that could
be a "lehver."

19
00:00:34,730 --> 00:00:37,160
Let's see, a "lehver,"
a "lehver"...

20
00:00:37,165 --> 00:00:38,565
Everybody hold on!

21
00:00:38,567 --> 00:00:40,297
(Sheldon:)Let's take this problem
one step at a time.

22
00:00:40,302 --> 00:00:41,972
(Sheldon:)First, we need to decide

23
00:00:41,970 --> 00:00:44,270
(Sheldon:)whether we're calling it
leever or lehver.

24
00:00:46,240 --> 00:00:48,170
(Sheldon:)And the sooner
we decide it's leever,

25
00:00:48,176 --> 00:00:51,046
(Sheldon:)the sooner we can roll up
our sleeves... not slehves...

26
00:00:51,046 --> 00:00:52,716
(Sheldon:)and get to work.

27
00:00:52,714 --> 00:00:58,024
(Leonard:)We're gonna be here
"foreever."

